  "_expect": "Fields in `expect` are what deterministic checks should find. max/checkin_over: dollar amounts (null = none said). stores: stores the shopper named ([] = none). must_haves: words the drafter should keep as features; not_must_haves: words it must not turn into a hard feature. quantity: how many items. conditions_of_sale: store terms to keep (free returns). deliver_by: words of the deadline (null = none). ship_to: a word of the destination (null = ships to the shopper). exact_item: only the item named. substitute_asked: the shopper's own words ask before a substitute. A field left out is not scored for that request (used where the request is ambiguous). warnings: readback warnings that should fire. unmapped: phrases that can't become rules. items: words that must appear in what to buy (so code can see a gift card, or both items). search_window: words of how long to keep looking (null = not said; a deadline is not a search window). new_store_asked: the shopper's own words ask before a new store. recurrence: one_time / weekly / monthly. budget: total across repeat buys.",
